.TH geectl-remote-create-token 1  "geectl-remote-create-token 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-create\-token \- Create an operation\-scoped trigger token for the authenticated user. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the creation. The secret prints once, at creation: store it now. Project and package go together: give both to scope the token to a package, or neither for a global token
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote create\-token\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-operation\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an operation\-scoped trigger token for the authenticated user. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the creation. The secret prints once, at creation: store it now. Project and package go together: give both to scope the token to a package, or neither for a global token
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-operation\fR \fI<OPERATION>\fR
The operation the token authorises: runservice, rebuild, release, or workflow
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
runservice: Run source services: the `runservice` trigger
.IP \(bu 2
rebuild: Rebuild packages: the `rebuild` trigger
.IP \(bu 2
release: Release packages: the `release` trigger
.IP \(bu 2
workflow: Run SCM/CI workflows: the `workflow` trigger
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The project of the package the token is scoped to
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package the token is scoped to
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
A description identifying the token, at most 64 characters
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
